From 4f3d3b761a2c0b56f21e34d971f4b021e8bc42e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William King <wking53214@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 09:56:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Roadster phase-1 final pieces: rate_limiter_v2.py (F-F) +
 circuit_breaker.py (F-A app-layer)

- circuit_breaker.py: per-resource breaker, no shared/global instance.
  Wired into production_harness.py at the two real call sites
  (Claude safety_check, ledger append_decision) per approved diff.
  Claude threshold 5/30s, Postgres 3/15s, 2 half-open successes to
  close. Added is_failure predicate support after finding
  safety_check() swallows exceptions and encodes failure in its
  return value -- an exception-only breaker there would never trip.

- rate_limiter_v2.py: Redis-backed token bucket, F-F fix (bucket by
  validated API key, never connecting IP). Attaches at api_server_v2's
  INGRESS_GUARDS seam ONLY when auth is configured -- an earlier
  unconditional wiring fell back to IP for unauthenticated traffic,
  which is F-F's exact defect reintroduced; fixed before landing.

- 29 new tests, all against real Redis/Postgres/api.anthropic.com,
  96/96 total across three clean runs (each suite its own process,
  matching this repo's established convention).

- Found, flagged, not fixed (out of this build's scope): sid_exists()
  has no exception handling at all (a full Postgres outage crashes
  process_call before reaching either breaker); operational_resilience
  .setup_logging() has no handler-dedup guard (worked around locally
  in circuit_breaker.py).

See roadster_breakers_verification_report_v1.md for full detail.
